WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.448
- [Woman] Wonderful, wonderful.

00:00:01.448 --> 00:00:04.031
(door banging)

00:00:05.239 --> 00:00:08.860
(police speaking in foreign language)

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.840
- [Narrator] This woman's
door was kicked in by police

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.169
when she refused to go to quarantine.

00:00:13.169 --> 00:00:14.820
(people speaking in foreign language)

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.000
Others in Shanghai
smashed rotten vegetables

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.630
in the street

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.390
and performed so-called concerts
with their pots and pans

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.730
to express their frustration

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.490
after weeks of life under lockdown

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.060
in China's most populous city

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.728
and economic capital.

00:00:27.728 --> 00:00:30.880
(pans banging)

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:31.930
- We have seen a lot of emotion,

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.649
a lot of people angry,

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:35.730
a lot of people sad, a
lot of people depressed,

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.910
a lot of people in despair.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.750
- [Narrator] In videos that
have bubbled up online,

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.090
despite censors' efforts
to take them down,

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:44.270
acts of disobedience,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.450
unusual for China, show new challenges

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:47.520
for China's authorities

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.240
as they double down their policy trying

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.723
to keep COVID-19 out of
the country completely.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.970
The city-wide lockdown began in late March

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.700
as Shanghai tackled
thousands of new cases a day,

00:00:58.700 --> 00:00:59.533
the biggest outbreak China

00:00:59.533 --> 00:01:01.940
has seen since the pandemic began.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.100
Some compounds had already
been in lockdown before that.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.437
- It's a city of 25 million people

00:01:07.437 --> 00:01:09.870
and we've seen this remarkable stream

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.770
of footage come out of Shanghai,

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:14.890
most of it filmed by ordinary people,

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:17.440
amateurs on their smartphones

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.020
but they do reflect frustrations

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:22.700
that we've all heard from
people who are living there.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:23.533
- [Narrator] In one video,

00:01:23.533 --> 00:01:25.658
a resident refused to
cooperate with officials.

00:01:25.658 --> 00:01:30.075
(woman speaking in foreign language)

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:34.321
(door banging)

00:01:34.321 --> 00:01:36.706
(man speaking in foreign language)

00:01:36.706 --> 00:01:39.440
(woman speaking in foreign language)

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:40.370
- [Narrator] The woman who filmed

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.810
and posted this video online
says she tested positive

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.560
but the test needed to be reviewed.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:48.800
Police eventually too
her away to quarantine.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.570
She didn't respond to requests for comment

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:51.460
but said in her post

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.310
that the police later fixed the door.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:55.860
For weeks, Shanghai residents

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.760
have expressed frustration online,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.750
but more protests have
recently taken place

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:00.952
in the physical world.

00:02:00.952 --> 00:02:03.340
(upbeat music)
(crockery banging)

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.960
Synchronized banging of crockery,

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.960
dubbed The Concerts, have been organized.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.150
This prompted the government

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.620
to accuse unspecified foreign conspirators

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:14.793
and warnings via WeChat and
loudspeaker announcements.

00:02:16.744 --> 00:02:21.494
(announcer speaking in foreign language)

00:02:34.729 --> 00:02:38.270
(woman speaking in foreign language)

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:39.290
- [Narrator] One sensitive issue

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.380
that has infuriated
citizens during the lockdown

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:43.140
has been the supply of food.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.230
These vegetables were
supposed to be distributed

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.310
to hungry families locked in their homes.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:48.663
Instead, they rotted.

00:02:49.706 --> 00:02:52.090
(people speaking in foreign language)

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:54.170
In this scene, people
can be seen complaining

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:57.660
to a police officer who
promises to investigate.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.140
These videos uploaded
on platforms like WeChat

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.760
and Weibo have been taken down

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.873
and re-uploaded a number of times.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.790
Authorities have promised more food

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:07.910
and vowed to punish those

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.910
who have made mistakes with supplies.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.660
At least three officials have been fired

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.133
for being slow to distribute food.

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:18.550
(Huang speaking in foreign language)

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.620
- [Narrator] These public flare-ups come

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.550
as lockdowns impact
businesses large and small.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.980
Factories for Tesla, Apple and many others

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.410
were shut down for periods of time

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.160
during the lockdown and companies warned

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.360
of disruptions to their supplies.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.550
And while some people living
and working in the city

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.220
have continued to receive a salary

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.200
from their employers,

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.430
others have been left without pay.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.200
- It's a very visible
and high-profile city.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.210
It's a city where you have
both blue collar workers.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:52.970
It's home to many of the
most important factories

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:54.810
in China producing autos

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.610
and producing a lot of other goods

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:57.650
that get shipped around the world.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:00.310
It has the world's largest port.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:03.980
You also have the white collar industries.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:06.653
Shanghai is the financial center of China.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:08.930
- [Narrator] After six weeks of lockdown

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.010
and a brief easing of
rules for some residents

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.730
to buy groceries and medicine,

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.260
authorities in Shanghai have
tightened restrictions again

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:18.250
even as COVID-19 cases in the city fall.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.130
Shanghai officials have thanked residents

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.193
for their understanding and cooperation.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.070
The head of the World Health Organization

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.790
said China should rethink its strategy

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.040
in a rare rebuke.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:33.040
- When we talk about
the zero COVID strategy,

00:04:33.538 --> 00:04:35.800
we don't think that it's sustainable,

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:37.750
considering the behavior of the virus now

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.113
and what we anticipate in the future.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.450
- [Narrator] Unswayed by the WHO,

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.910
China's sticking with its policy

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.150
of eradicating COVID-19 completely,

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.910
saying any relaxation of measures

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.196
could allow the virus to rebound.

00:04:50.196 --> 00:04:52.863
(pensive music)

